a and returned the compressed bytes.","aliasOf":"aiohttp.compression_utils.ZLibCompressor.compress"},{"path":"aiohttp.http_writer.ZLibCompressor.compress_sync","kind":"method","dispname":"compress_sync","docUri":null,"signature":"(self, data: collections.abc.Buffer) -> bytes","aliasOf":"aiohttp.compression_utils.ZLibCompressor.compress_sync"},{"path":"aiohttp.http_writer.ZLibCompressor.flush","kind":"method","dispname":"flush","docUri":null,"signature":"(self, mode: int | None = None) -> bytes","doc":"Flush the compressor synchronously.\n\n**WARNING: This method is NOT cancellation-safe when called after compress().**\nThe flush() operation accesses shared compressor state. If compress() was\ncancelled, calling flush() may result in corrupted data. The connection MUST\nbe closed after compress() cancellation.\n\nFor cancellation-safe compression (e.g., WebSocket), the caller MUST wrap\ncompress() + flush() + send operations in a shield and lock to ensure atomicity.","doc_summary":"Flush the compressor synchronously.","aliasOf":"aiohttp.compression_utils.ZLibCompressor.flush"}]}
